# Values that must never appear in a published tree, its history, or its commit messages.
#
# Copy this to .publish-denylist (gitignored) and replace the descriptions with the REAL values,
# one extended-regex per line. The real file is deliberately never committed: a denylist stored in
# the repo it protects publishes every secret it was written to catch.
#
# tools/preflight_publish.sh reads it and refuses to publish on a match.
#
# What belongs here:
#
#   - The real phone number, in every format it might appear in: bare 10 digits, hyphenated,
#     spaced, and the last-8 form. Check commit messages too, which a file scrub does not touch.
#   - Private hostnames for the backend and push endpoints.
#   - Deployment IPs, including any short-lived ones from an earlier host.
#   - Any bearer token or API key that was ever pasted into a file, even briefly -- git keeps it.
#   - Personal email addresses, if they should not be in the public log.
#   - Infrastructure LOGIN targets (login user and host names, SSH key filenames), not just service endpoints.
#     If a string would let someone try to log in somewhere, it belongs here.
#
# Anchor short numeric patterns as (^|[^0-9])NNNN([^0-9]|$) so hex digests do not match. Never write real digits into this committed file.
#
# Placeholders must not match themselves: anchor the pattern so a `<placeholder>` cannot match.
#
# Examples of the FORM (these are placeholders, not real values):
#
# 2405550101
# 240[-. ]?555[-. ]?0101
# 555-0101
# push\.example\.internal
# api\.example\.internal
# 203\.0\.113\.[0-9]+
# 198\.51\.100\.[0-9]+
# root@[0-9A-Za-z]
# (^|[^0-9])0101([^0-9]|$)     <- the anchored last-four form
# example_deploy_key
#
# Also list internal-process phrases here rather than in preflight_publish.sh: private repo or
# module names, first names, project code names, and any phrase that narrates a private decision.
